2026-09-28 — typed call-mode selection and named floating-interface refusals.

RED 1: floating-target-call-refusal.c CASE=0 reports E3101 on the preceding
compiler, not the existing E3049 contract. TargetBuiltin nominal floating
types missed function_value_type's Float branch and fell through to its
generic unsupported-type error. The shared function-interface classifier now
names the eight nominal GNU/Arm scalar floating types explicitly. It does NOT
alias them to equal-size float/double types, enable half/bfloat execution,
reclassify sizeless SVE types, or refuse pointers to ordinary object storage.

RED 2: the positive storage-pointer control independently exposes E3007 in the
C-HIR interpreter. The isolated unused-typed-call.c fails CASE=0,2,5,6 before
the repair: int*, double, adjusted array and function-pointer parameters.
The bodies do not read these parameters, and the actual arguments are integer
constants, so the old body-only scan wrongly selects the integer slot machine.
Call argument conversion/binding still needs a typed value. Requirements now
inspect reached definitions' canonical signatures as well as their bodies.
Aliases, transitive calls, void results and unreachable unsupported functions
are covered. Passing an uninitialized actual argument still reports E3001.

Focused lowering and CLI integration: 75 tests pass before the additional
reachability controls. Five signature forms x eight target float spellings
exercise the named refusal; the CLI exercises __fp16/__bf16 x five forms x
three modes x O0/O2. Pointer/layout controls pass both interpreters and emit.
Seven ordinary typed-call controls pass both interpreters; native GCC14,
Clang19 and EvoCC at O0/O2 give 42/42 passes. Two target-float pointer/layout
controls add 12/12 native passes, for 54/54 total.

Eight unchanged original floating-half-boundaries.c commands (KIND=1/2,
CASE=1, O0/O2, EvoIR/native emission) now refuse with E3049, not E3101.
This closes the diagnostic leak, NOT L03 execution or the larger campaign.
Existing source, options and exported sysroot paths are retained.

The first native attempt executed all 54 cases successfully but its final
compiler-identity guard FAILED because an overlapping Cargo rebuild replaced
the debug binary. It is retained under typed-call-20260928 and is not accepted.
The final attempt starts after binary construction, executes all 54 cases and
passes the before/after identity guard. The frozen kernel compiler is separate
and unchanged; no kernel or library objects were installed by these tests.

